**Finding: COMPLIANT (preferred position met) — no redline proposed.**

The Agreement contains no non-solicitation, no-hire, or anti-poaching covenant binding AbbVie (or Harpoon). Targeted searches for "solicit"/"solicitation", "recruit", "induce", "no-hire", "employ or engage", and "non-compete"/restrictive covenant returned no responsive clauses. The only personnel-facing provisions are:

- **§ 10.4.1 / § 10.3.4** — mutual covenants to obtain invention-assignment and confidentiality rights from Affiliates, sublicensees, employees and agents;
- **§ 10.2.14** — debarment representations concerning employees/agents;
- **§ 2 / § 4** — employees attending JSC meetings and manufacturing meetings;
- **§ 9** — confidentiality flow-downs to officers, directors, employees and agents.

None restricts either Party from soliciting or hiring the other's personnel, so AbbVie carries no restrictive covenant. This sits at the playbook's preferred position ("No non-solicit on Customer"), so no fallback narrowing (mutuality, 12-month limit, advertising and unsolicited-approach carve-outs) is needed. We should simply resist any attempt to add such a covenant in later drafts.
